// THE PROCESS'S CODE PAGE IS UTF-8 (docs/spec/llvm.md §2, mastretire-2026-11-03).
// Win32's `A` functions read a string's bytes in the process's ANSI code page,
// and the language's strings are UTF-8, so the two agree exactly when the code
// page is 65001. The windows target embeds a manifest that declares it; without
// it the code page is the system's (1252 here), and `CreateFileA("tést.txt")`
// named a file `tÃ©st.txt`.
use win/WinNls as n
use win/print

export fn main() { print.print_int(n.GetACP()) }
